{"format":1,"seq":40,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the issue now: with a grammar-constrained custom tool on openai-codex, the model emits a plain function_call with raw text arguments instead of a custom_tool_call, so Pi's openai-responses parser fails to JSON-parse it. The fix would be recovering by mapping that raw input into a `{code}` structure, so I want to trace through pi-ai's code to find where this parsing happens.\n\nI'm also noticing a separate rendering issue: Pi's streaming row keeps stale args from the partial `{}` state, and message_end doesn't seem to update the row's args properly. There's also a question of whether displaying applied @pit options plus validation in the header is really part of this fix or a separate feature I should check against the current displayArguments logic in the renderer.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01SwRoUGkvomHFCmyFXMQMGF","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Read renderer displayArguments and search Pi for Received arguments handling\"}\nasync ({ workspace: { search }, shell: { exec } }) => {\n  const [d, p] = await Promise.all([\n    search(\"displayArguments\", { path: \"src\", contextLines: 8, limit: 20 }),\n    exec(\"grep -rn 'Received arguments' node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-ai/dist | head; grep -rn 'argumentsError' node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/dist --include=*.js -l | head; grep -rn 'grammarToolInputProperties\\\\|custom_tool_call' node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-ai/dist/api/*.js | head -40\"),\n  ]);\n  return { d, p: p.stdout };\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":610,"cacheRead":37389,"cacheWrite":421,"totalTokens":38422,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":287},"stopReas